Subject: [CKI] Allocation adjustment as per BSA Decrease from SNRF1315W/E

TO : All concerned offices
CC : CTS, COV, CCE, ASI, WSI
FM : CTY - AE

As we already informed through the other channels,
please be notfied that BSA of CKI will be consistently decreased effective from SNRF1315W/E,
which means that all loading offices's QTA and actual loading volumes should be down fitting into total BSA.

This has been made at short notice due to the stake in the space swap between Indonesia lanes with our partners,
please seek your understanding and refer to the guideline.
[cid:image010.jpg@01CEE9FE.5E3BDEB0]

As BSA will be decreased from 200 Teus to 100 Teus, QTA will be adjusted from CCE/ASI soon,
however all loading offices are adivsed in advance to follow the instruction below in order to prevent any confusion for cargoes handling.

* SELBB & SHABB : The allocation has been down, please divert the cargoe to NCI/HNNB0064W
                         We will allocate more as the deducted portion onto NCI/HNNB0064W

* NBOBB : Due to the limited network to JKT, we will remain the current alloation, however to utilize the space fully,
             check the f'cast and then make a correct f'cast.

Copy to CCE/ASI/WSI

- Please promptly adjust the QTA by each office on CKI within the BSA and infrom to all office.
  When you make a new QTA, please refer to the factors below.

  1. As you know well, NBOBB don't have any option for Indonesia service except for CKI
  2. On CKI, the minimum space to SHA should be allocated by considering into some customers like Philps's loading and no show ratio.
  3. Due to the limited network from KHH to PUS for TPEBB, at least 60 teus on weekly basis should be guaranteed on Yield MGMT Concept under the tough situation


Please contact CTY - AE if you have a question.
Your prompt handling and sincere cooperation would be appreciated.


Tks & B.rgds






